  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nI was surprised to realize that `<input type=email>` doesn't support `selectionStart` / `selectionEnd` / `select()` in Gecko. Turns out that's per spec: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#concept-input-apply\n\nhttps://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=12262 was filed ages ago and closed with the following reasoning:\n\n> Rationale: The type=email case isn't supposed to show a simple text edit box, especially when multiple=\"\" is applied. Browsers might do it now, but I expect this will change in due course, as they one-up each other on the UI experience here.\n\nHowever years have passed and UI hasn't really changed. Instead, browsers have added autofill for usernames and passwords. Should we recognize reality and make these APIs apply to `<input type=email>`? There's [one test](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/forms/textfieldselection?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=html%2Fsemantics%2Fforms%2Ftextfieldselection%2Fselection-not-application.html) for this that we'd have to change really.\n\ncc @annevk @whatwg/forms ",
